# ── Game content — NEVER commit ──────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenKingdoms ships no game data. These patterns are a safety net, not the
# policy; see docs/ASSETS.md. An asset committed to a public repo is a
# takedown risk and is effectively permanent once cloned.
*.hpi
*.gp3
*.ufo
*.ccx
*.gaf
*.taf
*.3do
*.cob
*.tnt
*.sct
*.pcx
data/
extracted/
game-data/
**/gamedata/
*.bnk
*.wav
*.ogg
*.mp3
*.bik
*.smk

# Emscripten data bundles (these pack game content into the wasm build)
*.data
*.data.js

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
Testing/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.wasm
*.wasm.map

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Local config and captures ────────────────────────────────────────────
